ppens to be importable, but static analysis and readers are misled.\n\nAlso, the three notification messages in `check_endpoints_loop` (`[OK] RECOVERED`, `[ALERT] DOWN`, `[WARNING] STILL DOWN`) all hand-format `\"...\n\nDashboard: {config.DASHBOARD_URL}\"` inline. Extract a small helper.\n\n## What to change (ONLY this file)\n1. Change the parameter annotation on `update_notification_time` from `requests.structures.CaseInsensitiveDict` to `sqlite3.Cursor`. Add `import sqlite3` at the top; drop the unused import chain if no other use of `requests.structures` remains (there is not one).\n2. Add a small local helper `_format_alert(kind: str, url: str, status: int) -> str` (module-private, above `check_endpoints_loop`) that returns the message with the dashboard footer. Use it in all three scenarios inside `check_endpoints_loop` so future footer changes happen in one place.\n3. Do not change any log strings, control flow, timing, or DB queries. Behavior must be byte-for-byte identical in message TEXT; only the assembly path changes.\n\n## Files you own\n`app/core/monitoring.py` \u2014 nothing else.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `grep -n \"CaseInsensitiveDict\" app/core/monitoring.py` returns nothing.\n- `grep -n \"import sqlite3\" app/core/monitoring.py` finds the new import.\n- `grep -n \"_format_alert\" app/core/monitoring.py` shows the helper is defined and called at least 3 times.\n- `python -c \"import app.core.monitoring\"` exits 0.","response":"Completed: Fix wrong type annotation in monitoring.py and unify dashboard message formatting","word_vector":{"backend":0.003968253968253968,"fix":0.003968253968253968,"wrong":0.003968253968253968,"type":0.003968253968253968,"annotation":0.011904761904761904,"in":0.01984126984126984,"monitoring":0.027777777777777776,"py":0.023809523809523808,"and":0.011904761904761904,"unify":0.003968253968253968,"dashboard":0.011904761904761904,"message":0.011904761904761904,"formatting":0.003968253968253968,"app":0.023809523809523808,"core":0.02380