+{"id": "3bb9834b5dc9", "title": "Set up pytest infrastructure with initial unit tests", "description": "Stand up a real test harness so subsequent refactors can be verified. There is currently no pytest setup \u2014 only an ad-hoc script `test_group_notifications.py`.\n\n## What to build\n1. `requirements-dev.txt` with: `pytest`, `pytest-cov`, `requests-mock`.\n2. `pytest.ini` at repo root with `testpaths = tests`, `pythonpath = .`, and `filterwarnings = ignore::DeprecationWarning`.\n3. `tests/__init__.py` (empty) and `tests/unit/__init__.py` (empty).\n4. `tests/conftest.py` \u2014 provide a `tmp_db_path` fixture that sets `DB_PATH` env var to a tempfile before importing `app.db`, and yields the path. Also provide an `initialized_db` fixture that calls `app.db.init_db()`.\n5. `tests/unit/test_url_validation.py` \u2014 cover `app.api.endpoints.validate_url` and `normalize_url`: valid domain, valid domain with port, invalid port (out of range, non-numeric), IPv4, localhost, missing scheme (gets https:// prepended), unsupported scheme (ftp://).\n6. `tests/unit/test_monitoring_helpers.py` \u2014 cover `app.core.monitoring.should_send_down_notification` (fresh notification when last_notified is None, blocked when within interval, allowed when past interval, allowed when last_notified is malformed).\n\n## Files you own\nOnly create files under `tests/`, and the two top-level config files. Do NOT edit any files in `app/`.\n\n## Acceptance\n`pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt && pytest -x -q` exits 0 and shows at least 10 passing tests.", "role": "qa", "priority": 0, "scope": "medium", "complexity": "medium", "estimated_minutes": 240, "status": "done", "task_type": "standard", "upgrade_details": null, "depends_on": [], "parent_task_id": null, "depends_on_repo": null, "owned_files": ["tests/__init__.py", "tests/conftest.py", "tests/unit/__init__.py", "tests/unit/test_url_validation.py", "tests/unit/test_monitoring_helpers.py", "requirements-dev.txt", "p